course: dictionary
lesson: 736
title: Bask: warm in the sun, or glow with praise
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: «Bask» is a verb, so it describes an action. To bask means to lie or sit enjoying warmth, especially sunlight. «Butterflies need a body temperature of about 30 degrees to fly well, so they bask in the sun.» The clue is the warmth: butterflies need heat, so bask must mean soaking up warmth.
explain: Bask has a second meaning: to enjoy attention, praise or success. A team that wins the cup can bask in the glory. You cannot sit in glory, so here bask means enjoying it. Check your meaning by swapping in enjoy: the team can enjoy the glory, so it fits.
explain: Animals that are cold-blooded use the sun to warm up. «Crocodiles are cold-blooded: they bask in the sun to warm up» tells you why they do it. When a crocodile gapes its mouth while basking, heat escapes and it cools down. It is not a yawn.
fact: Bask is a verb, and its forms are bask, basks, basked and basking.
fact: «Bask» means to lie or sit enjoying warmth, especially sunlight.
fact: «Bask» can also mean to enjoy attention, praise or success, as in bask in the glory.
fact: Cold-blooded animals such as lizards, snakes and turtles bask to warm up.
fact: Turtles bask in the sun to warm up and to make vitamin D for strong shells.
exercise: «Butterflies need a body temperature of about 30 degrees to fly well, so they bask in the sun.» What does bask mean here? | Sleep under a leaf | Flap their wings very fast | *Lie in the sun to soak up warmth | Hide in the shade
exercise: Ella says, «The actor basked in the applause after the show.» What does basked mean? | Forgot all the lines | Got very cold | Ran away from the crowd | *Enjoyed the praise and attention
exercise: «Crocodiles bask with their mouths open.» Why do they gape their mouths while basking? | To catch flies | To sing to other crocodiles | *To let heat escape and cool down | To yawn at the sun
test: What is the main reason lizards and snakes bask in the sun? | To hide from other animals | To catch fish | *To warm up, because they are cold-blooded | To make their shells strong
test: Which phrase means enjoying success and praise? | Hide in the glory | Drift in the dark | Bask in the cold mud | *Bask in the glory
exam: «The lizard basked on a warm rock all afternoon.» What does basked mean? | Dug a hole to hide | Ate a large meal | Ran around in the cold | *Sat in the warmth of the sun
